task.translation_caching {
  action (completed) {
    - create a ./cache directory, it should be added to .gitignore so that it won't be committed to git repo
    - under the ./cache directory, it should be subfolders for each book's guttenberg id, for example: pg2701, under this subfolder, stored the translated text in file named p_{paragraph_offset}_simplified.txt, also have a file p_{paragraph_offset}_progress.txt {
      when a paragraph is being translated, record the percentage number (1-100) to p_{paragraph_offset}_progress.txt
    }

    - when we load the book, first look at the ./cache directory and load the corresponding content of p_{paragraph_offset}_progress.txt if p_{paragraph_offset}_progress.txt has 100 in it (meaning this paragraph is fully translated), otherwise, send the paragraph to llm to translate and cache it
  }
}

